BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.955
2026 Page 1 of 318
1 H.955
2 Introduced by Committee on Education
3 Date:
4 Subject: Education; school districts; cooperative education service areas; union
5 school districts; education finance; prekindergarten education
6 Statement of purpose of bill as introduced: This bill proposes to (1) rename
7 boards of cooperative education services to cooperative educational services
8 areas; (2) assign each supervisory union to a cooperative educational service
9 area; (3) require all school districts to participate in a study committee to study
10 the advisability of forming a unified union school district; (4) amend the
11 contingent effective dates in 2025 Acts and Resolves No. 73; and (5) require
12 JFO to hire a contractor to make recommendations regarding how to account
13 for the provision of prekindergarten education within Vermont’s education
14 finance system.
15 An act relating to next steps in transforming Vermont’s education system
16 It is hereby enacted by the General Assembly of the State of Vermont:
17 * * * Legislative Intent * * *
18 Sec. 1. LEGISLATIVE INTENT
19 (a) To ensure each student is provided substantially equal educational
20 opportunities that will prepare the student to thrive in a 21st-century world, it

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.955
2026 Page 2 of 318
1 is the intent of the General Assembly to work strategically, intentionally, and
2 thoughtfully to ensure that each incremental change made to Vermont’s public
3 education system provides strength and support to its only constitutionally
4 required governmental service.
5 (b) The General Assembly recognizes that Vermont’s schools anchor local
6 economies and community identity, connecting young people to their homes
7 while supporting workforce development and long-term stability, and that
8 different regions of Vermont have different needs, challenges, and
9 opportunities. Further, it is the intent of the General Assembly to ensure that
10 local voice and community input retain an important role in Vermont’s
11 evolving education landscape.
12 * * * Cooperative Educational Service Areas * * *
13 Sec. 2. 16 V.S.A. chapter 10 is amended to read:
14 CHAPTER 10. BOARDS OF COOPERATIVE EDUCATION SERVICES
15 EDUCATIONALSERVICE AREAS
16 § 601. POLICY
17 It is the policy of the State to allow and encourage supervisory unions to
18 create boards of cooperative education services educational service areas to
19 provide shared programs and services on a regional and statewide level.
20 Formation of a board of cooperative education services shall be designed to
21 build upon the geographically focused cooperative regions used by Vermont

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.955
2026 Page 3 of 318
1 superintendents as of July 1, 2024; It is the intent of the General Assembly that
2 cooperative educational service areas are utilized by member supervisory
3 unions to maximize the impact of available dollars through collaborative
4 funding; reduce duplication of programs, personnel, and services; and
5 contribute to equalizing the equalization of educational opportunities for all
6 pupils.
7 § 602. DEFINITIONS
8 As used in this chapter:
9 (1) “Educator” means any:
10 (A) individual licensed under chapter 51 of this title, the majority of
11 whose employed time in a public school district, supervisory union, or board
12 of cooperative education services educational service area is assigned to
13 furnish to students direct instructional or other educational services, as defined
14 by rule of the Standards Board, or who is otherwise subject to licensing as
15 determined by the Standards Board; or
16 * * *
17 (3) “Cooperative educational service area” or “CESA” means an
18 association of supervisory unions created pursuant to this chapter to deliver
19 shared programs and services to complement the educational programs of
20 member supervisory unions in a cost-effective manner. A CESA shall be a

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.955
2026 Page 4 of 318
1 body politic and corporate with the powers and duties afforded it under this
2 chapter.
3 § 603. CREATION OF BOARD OF COOPERATIVE EDUCATION
4 SERVICES EDUCATIONALSERVICE AREAS;
5 ORGANIZATION; SECRETARY APPROVAL
6 (a) Establishment of boards of cooperative education services educational
7 service areas. When the boards of two or more supervisory unions vote to
8 explore the advisability of entering into a written agreement to provide shared
9 programs and services, the interested boards shall meet and discuss the terms
10 of any such agreement. At this meeting or a subsequent meeting, the
11 participating boards may enter into a proposed agreement to form an
12 association of supervisory unions to deliver shared programs and services to
13 complement the educational programs of member supervisory unions in a cost-
14 effective manner. An association formed pursuant to this chapter shall be
15 known as a board of cooperative education services (BOCES) and shall be a
16 body politic and corporate with the powers and duties afforded them under this
17 chapter. Supervisory unions are arranged into the following cooperative
18 educational service areas:
19 (1) The Champlain Valley North CESA is formed of the member
20 supervisory unions of:

