7 (b) Articles of agreement Bylaws. Agreements to form a BOCES pursuant
8 to this chapter shall take the form of articles of agreement and shall serve as
9 the operating agreement for a BOCES. Agreements shall include a cost-
10 benefit analysis outlining the projected financial savings or enhanced
11 outcomes, or both, that the parties expect to realize through shared services or
12 programs. No agreement or subsequent amendments shall take effect unless
13 approved by the member supervisory union boards and the Secretary of
14 Education. The Secretary shall approve articles of agreement if the Secretary
15 finds that the formation of the proposed BOCES is in the best interests of the
16 State, the students, and the member supervisory unions and aligns with the
17 policy set forth in section 601 of this title, subject to the limitations of
18 subsection (d) of this section. Each CESA shall establish bylaws to serve as
19 the operating agreement of the CESA. At a minimum, the articles of
20 agreement bylaws shall state:
21 (1) the names of the participating supervisory unions;

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.955
2026 Page 12 of 318
1 (2) the mission, purpose, and focus of the BOCES CESA;
2 (3) the programs or services to be offered by the BOCES CESA;
3 (4) the financial terms and conditions of membership of the BOCES
4 CESA, including any applicable membership fee;
5 (5) the service fees for member supervisory unions and the service fees
6 for nonmember supervisory unions, as applicable;
7 (6) the detailed procedure for the preparation and adoption of an annual
8 budget with carryforward provisions;
9 (7) the method of termination of the BOCES and the withdrawal of
10 member supervisory unions, which shall include the apportionment of assets
11 and liabilities; [Repealed.]
12 (8) the procedure for admitting new members and for amending the
13 articles of agreement bylaws;
14 (9) the powers and duties of the board of directors of the BOCES CESA
15 to operate and manage the association, including:
16 (A) board meeting attendance requirements;
17 (B) consequences for failure to attend a board meeting;
18 (C) a conflict-of-interest policy; and
19 (D) a policy regarding board member salaries or stipends; and
20 (10) any other matter not incompatible with law that the member
21 supervisory unions consider necessary to the formation of the BOCES.

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.955
2026 Page 13 of 318
1 (c) Board of directors. A BOCES CESA shall be managed by a board of
2 directors, which shall be composed of one person appointed annually by each
3 member supervisory union board. Appointed persons shall be members of a
4 member supervisory union board or the superintendent or designee of the
5 member supervisory union. Each member of the BOCES CESA board of
6 directors shall be entitled to a vote. No member of the board of directors of a
7 BOCES CESA shall serve as a member of a board of directors or as an officer
8 or employee of any related for-profit or nonprofit organization. The board of
9 directors shall elect a chair from its members and provide for such other
10 officers as it may determine are necessary. The board of directors may also
11 establish subcommittees and create board policies and procedures as it may
12 determine are necessary. The board of directors shall meet not fewer than four
13 times annually. Each member of the board of directors shall provide updates
14 on the activities of the BOCES CESA on a quarterly basis to the member’s
15 appointing supervisory union board at an open board meeting.
16 (d) Number of BOCESs. There shall be not more than seven BOCESs
17 statewide. Supervisory unions shall not be a member of more than one
18 BOCES but may seek services as a nonmember from other BOCESs.
19 [Repealed.]

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.955
