1 § 606. ANNUALREPORT; PUBLIC INFORMATION
2 (a) The board of a BOCES CESA shall prepare an annual report
3 concerning the affairs of the BOCES CESA and have it printed and distributed
4 to the boards of the member supervisory unions. The annual report shall
5 include, at a minimum:
6 (1) information on the programs and services offered by the BOCES
7 CESA, including information on the cost-effectiveness of such programs and
8 services and progress made towards achieving the objectives and purposes set
9 forth in the articles of agreement; and
10 (2) audited financial statements and the independent auditor’s report.
11 (b) A BOCES CESA shall maintain an internet website that makes the
12 following information available to the public at no cost:
13 (1) a list of the members of the board of directors of the BOCES CESA;
14 (2) copies of approved minutes of open meetings held by the board of
15 the BOCES CESA;
16 (3) a copy of the articles of agreement and any subsequent amendments;
17 and
18 (4) a copy of the annual report required under subsection (a) of this
19 section.

