1 * * * Union School District Exploration and Formation * * *
2 Sec. 13. UNION SCHOOLDISTRICT CREATION CONSULTATION AND
3 FACILITATION
4 (a) Facilitator. On or before October 1, 2026, the Vermont Learning
5 Collaborative (VTLC), a CESA formed pursuant to 16 V.S.A. chapter 10, shall
6 employ or contract for the services of seven union school district formation
7 facilitators (facilitators) who shall be responsible for organizing and
8 facilitating study committees to study the advisability of forming a unified
9 union school district. The VTLC shall also hire one lead facilitator who, in
10 addition to facilitating study committees as necessary, shall oversee the work
11 of the seven facilitators. A facilitator shall have knowledge of and experience
12 working in Vermont’s public education system. The VTLC shall assign one
13 facilitator to each CESA membership region created pursuant to 16 V.S.A.
14 § 603(a)(1)–(7).
15 (b) Study committees.
16 (1) On or before December 1, 2026:
(A) Each facilitator shall group school districts within the
facilitator’s assigned CESA region’s member supervisory unions together to
form study committees to study the advisability of forming a unified union
school district. The facilitator shall consult with school district boards prior to
finalizing study committee membership. Using the suggested school district

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.955
2026 Page 29 of 318
groupings contained in Sec. 14 as guidance, and taking into consideration
grand list values, accounting for the homestead exemption and current
education spending, the facilitator shall group school districts together
according to the following criteria:
1 (i) total average daily membership of school districts forming a
2 study committee shall be a minimum of 2,000 students, as practical;
3 (ii) school districts shall be contiguous; and
4 (iii) school districts on the same study committee may be
5 members of different supervisory unions.
6 (B) Each study committee shall hold its first meeting.
7 (2) Notwithstanding any provision of law to the contrary, a school
8 district shall participate in the study committee it is assigned to by the
9 facilitator.
10 (3) A study committee formed pursuant to this section shall adhere to
11 the processes and requirements of 16 V.S.A. chapter 11, subchapter 2.
12 (A) A study committee formed pursuant to this section may identify
13 necessary or advisable school districts, as those terms are used in 16 V.S.A.
14 § 708(b)(1) and (2), that are not members of the study committee or are not
15 members of the CESA, or both, and shall work with the applicable facilitator
16 or facilitators to adjust study committee membership as necessary.

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.955
2026 Page 30 of 318
1 (B) Notwithstanding 16 V.S.A. § 706(b) as it applies to study
2 committee budgets and 16 V.S.A. § 707(a) and (b), a study committee formed
3 pursuant to this section shall be funded through appropriations made by the
4 General Assembly for this purpose; provided, however, that if a study
5 committee’s needs exceed the appropriations provided, it may elect to increase
6 its budget according to the processes and procedures established in 16 V.S.A.
7 chapter 11.
8 (C) In addition to the requirements of 16 V.S.A. chapter 11,
9 subchapter 2, a study committee shall also explore the advisability and
10 feasibility of a contemplated new unified union school district operating a
11 regional middle or high school, or both. A regional middle or high school
12 contemplated pursuant to this section shall offer resident students increased
13 educational opportunities and access to career technical education.
14 (D) If a study committee formed pursuant to this section determines
15 that it is advisable to propose formation of a new unified union school district,
16 in addition to the report requirements in 16 V.S.A. § 708(c), the final report of
17 the study committee shall include an analysis of the following:
18 (i) the educational advantages and disadvantages likely to result
19 from the formation of the proposed unified union school district;
20 (ii) the financial advantages and disadvantages likely to result
21 from the formation of the proposed unified union school district;

