1 (iii) the likely operational and financial viability and sustainability
2 of the proposed new unified union school district; and
3 (iv) any other advantages or disadvantages of formation of the
4 proposed unified union school district, including any advantages or
5 disadvantages to the students and taxpayers of the region and the State.
6 (E)(i) If a study committee formed pursuant to this section
7 determines that it is inadvisable to propose formation of a new unified union
8 school district, before the study committee members vote to dissolve the study
9 committee pursuant to 16 V.S.A. § 708(d), the study committee shall prepare a
