13 (II) an analysis of the strengths and challenges of the current
14 structures of all “necessary” and “advisable” school districts;
15 (III) the reasons why formation of a new unified union school
16 district would be inadvisable, with specific references to any State law or rule
17 the study committee found to be an impediment to the formation of a unified
18 union school district, with a specific analysis of why such rule or law was an
19 impediment; and
20 (IV) if the decision of the study committee was not unanimous,
21 an analysis of the minority view of the committee outlining the ways in which

