9 Sec. 15. STUDY COMMITTEE RESULTS AND ANALYSIS;
10 FACILITATOR REPORT
11 On or before January 1, 2029, the lead facilitator employed or contracted by
12 the Vermont Learning Collaborative (VTLC) shall submit a written report to
13 the House and Senate Committees on Education with the results of each study
14 committee overseen by each facilitator employed or contracted by the VTLC
15 and information regarding whether, and if so, how, the following issues
16 impacted or influenced the final outcome for each study committee overseen
17 by the facilitator, along with recommendations for legislative action needed to
18 remove identified barriers to the formation of new union school districts:
19 (1) differences in staffing costs and the costs associated with moving
20 from several different collectively bargained agreements to one collectively
21 bargained agreement for applicable staff in the new union school district;

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.955
2026 Page 39 of 318
1 (2) differences in operating structures;
2 (3) geographic and topographic barriers;
3 (4) enrollment patterns and projections; and
4 (5) any other factor the facilitator found to have influenced the final
5 decision of a study committee.
6 Sec. 16. SUPERVISORY UNION AND CESA BOUNDARIES; AGENCY
7 OF EDUCATION REPORT
8 On or before January 1, 2029, the Agency of Education, in consultation
9 with the study committees formed pursuant to this act and the State Board of
10 Education, shall submit a written report to the House and Senate Committees
11 on Education with recommendations for supervisory union boundary
12 adjustments and CESA boundary adjustments that take into account the new
13 union school districts formed or proposed to be formed pursuant to this act.
