Sec. 27. INTRADISTRICT BUDGETING; AGENCY OF EDUCATION;
DISTRICT QUALITY STANDARDS; RULEMAKING
The Agency of Education shall, unless extended by the Legislative
Committee on Administrative Rules, adopt updates to the district quality
standards contained in Agency of Education, District Quality Standards (CVR
22-000-039) to establish criteria for intradistrict budgeting, pursuant to
3 V.S.A. § 843 on or before March 31, 2027. The criteria shall provide
guidelines for intradistrict budgeting that ensure resources are allocated
across schools within each district in a way that supports the State’s goal that
“all Vermont children will be afforded educational opportunities that are
substantially equal in quality” and enable them to achieve or exceed the
education quality standards approved by the State Board of Education.
